Package: simple-ca
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         adduser
Description: Small certificate authority with an HTTP server, ACME and a signing API
 simple-ca keeps a root CA and its issuing CAs in a directory, issues and
 revokes certificates and publishes CRLs. Its serve command publishes the CA
 certificates and CRLs over HTTP, with an ACME server, a signing API for
 tokens, and pages for tokens, certificates and the audit log.
 .
 The package installs simple-ca, the signing API clients request-cert,
 token-setup and request-jwt, and simple-ca-trust, which adds a root CA to
 the trust store. The units simple-ca.service, simple-ca-crl.service and
 simple-ca-crl.timer run as the user simple-ca on the CA in /etc/simple-ca;
 they are not enabled on install.
